findings.problem:
The Admission section is 'plan 23's verdict rule for Phase C'. It amends P23:269, which says a contract enters only if its development verdict is *works* 'under the rule the registration will use (Phase D3)'. The bound rule says that for development verdicts 'the bounded one counts' and that it is 'the dry run of the rule that the registration will carry into Phase D3'. Neither text says whether admission uses the recorded rule (2c rule, leave-one-out rule, passed check) or its bounded version. That is the decision the amendment exists to fix before outcomes, and it can be settled either way after the results are seen.

If the bound applies, it cannot be computed for the runs admission rests on. The bound scales 'the sample share' per run, but none of these runs has author or V4 codes:
- the three WD runs and the three fresh A1 runs (2c);
- the C and A1′ runs (Step 4);
- the A2 leave-one-out harness variants.

The A2 'on/off contrast' comparator (A2 minus the contract) is also uncoded. In addition, 'for unsampled A0 cases, the model pre-code is used where it is higher' has nothing to compare against: A0 now has no author sample at all (line 269), so this is a leftover from draft 2.

The principle is stated for every loss, but only about half of each A1/A2 run's 59–64 cases are coded (30 per run). Several groups get no state:
- A0 cases get a model pre-code only;
- the WD, fresh A1, C and A1′ runs are not coded at all;
- Step 5 runs other than 3b's r1 are not coded at all.

Uncoded losses reach no state individually. They enter only through the bound rule's scaled shares.

